            {
                "entry_id": "4eb186ab-d137-3802-8a3b-47f356283803",
                "word": "glam",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4fd9fb2f-ff03-3efd-9c62-e456de28024a",
                        "entry_id": "4eb186ab-d137-3802-8a3b-47f356283803",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Glamour; glamorousness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1aed038b-dccb-4873-a4af-741b774f5f7a",
                                "sense_id": "4fd9fb2f-ff03-3efd-9c62-e456de28024a",
                                "text": "Who wouldn’t be a glamor girl, a certain-to-enamor girl?\nWhat joie de vivre in her life is given her to cram,\nThe dinkum sex-appealing girl, the subtle-charm-revealing girl,\n’Mong men the havoc-dealing girl—in short, the girl with glam.!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "736abc0e-d249-3902-8b1c-c86c89a8b47d",
                        "entry_id": "4eb186ab-d137-3802-8a3b-47f356283803",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ellipsis of glam rock, the fashion and culture associated with this genre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "ellipsis",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1e555e8-cea1-4324-9260-54ba773db574",
                                "sense_id": "736abc0e-d249-3902-8b1c-c86c89a8b47d",
                                "text": "Blokes sporting make-up and vertiginous platform boots, songs that were precision-tooled melodramas of bubblegum pop and football-terrace stomp, a belief in pop itself as a liberating space for fantasy and shape-shifting: it’s perhaps unsurprising that glam, in whose rise Bowie played a huge part, has never been taken very seriously."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
